$DIR/main.p:26:14: b was moved into take2 (its parameter takes a Buf by value) at line 27, but the deferred call (line 26) uses it when the function returns
    Buf is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it when they
    are dropped. Passing an owner by value moves it instead of copying it, so
    that what it owns has exactly one owner. Since line 27, b holds nothing. The
    call deferred at line 26 keeps a view of b in its receiver or arguments and
    runs when the function returns, after line 27, so it would look at what b no
    longer holds.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    Give b a new value after line 27, so that the deferred call finds one:
        b = Buf{}
    Or do the work of the deferred call at the end of the function, before line
    27, instead of deferring it
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3301" for a longer explanation)
